WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.190
<b>May 25th   10:00 AM   Hakata</b>

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.230
Banba Private Investigations

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.230
He was sniffing around our business.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.460
He's an eyesore.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.250
Get rid of him tonight.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.940
No, thanks.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.620
I'm not gonna do any jobs until you pay up.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.330
I'm on strike.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.040
Why, you...

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.360
I can easily find someone
else to do this job!

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.460
Oh, yeah?

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.440
Whoever it is, they must
really be something.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.260
Why don't you ask them, then?

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.910
Though, I'll just end up killing them...

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:39.890
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.230
Long story short, a hitman should 
be showing up here any time now.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.060
And I'm going to kill them.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.440
Don't worry.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.400
I'll protect you, too.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.820
Of course, if the money issue gets 
resolved, it'll be a different story.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.970
Fine.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.250
Now leave, would you?

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.770
<b>#02 Irregular</b>

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.650
So he's still here, and asleep now.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:40.470
Soon, Qiaomei...

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.980
And he's even talking in his sleep.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:46.890
This killer's definitely got balls.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.980
Oh, are you awake?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.650
Hi, Murase Jun-kun.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.160
Oh, don't mind him.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.090
This guy tortured and killed a cat.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:10.870
We're avenging it, at its owner's request,

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:14.840
using the exact same 
methods he used on the cat.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.310
I'm an avenger.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.810
I exact vengeance on behalf of my clients.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.270
It was okay to decapitate 
him at the end, right?

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.920
Also, he didn't have a tail,

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.190
so I chopped off something else.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.650
Well done.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.430
Good job, Maru-chan.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.390
So he's the next one up?

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.960
Oh, hang on.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.120
I want to ask him something first.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:54.830
It's about your friends who were with 
you when you assaulted the foreigner.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.710
I'm not Murase!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:57.630
I'm Saito!

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.590
Huh?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.150
This is a misunderstanding!

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.860
I'd snuck in to kill Murase Jun!

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.510
I work for Murder, Inc!

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.820
Murder, Inc...

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.520
The contract killing company?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.940
M-My business card's in my breast pocket!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.690
Red Rum, Inc.  
Fukuoka Branch
Sales Division

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.270
Oh, my.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:22.660
He's telling the truth.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.210
But if we had the wrong guy,
then the real Murase Jun is...

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:34.250
I guess that was a little
too much gunpowder.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.700
Oh, well.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.210
The cops will work with us on that, anyway.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.100
Oh, Munakata-san?

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:47.180
Yoshida Masaki, Yamashiro Tatsuya, and 
Murase Jun have all been dealt with.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.890
Yes, as instructed, I made 
it look like a DUI accident.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.600
You can't really pass 
that off as an accident.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.940
Are we done with the idiot 
son's idiot friends?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.030
Yeah, and what a chore that was.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.910
So we're supposed to buy him women now?

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.920
Those were the mayor's orders.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.240
We have no choice.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:13.990
I'll talk to the organization 
tomorrow morning.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.380
Here's my business card.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.760
If you ever want revenge, give me a call.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:25.470
I'll give you a discount.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.930
Thank you.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.750
I might be in over my head in this city.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.890
What's wrong, Yamato? It's awfully 
early in the morning to call.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.840
Hey.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.330
Where are you sneaking off 
to without saying a word?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.040
Why? I'm not allowed to leave?

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.170
You're a target.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.960
It's dangerous to go outside.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.130
What's this?

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.650
Okay, you go buy it, then.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.150
Get the regular kind from 
Fukuya. No added coloring.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.600
Huh? What're you talking about?

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:17.020
Spicy pollock roe. My stock for today ran out.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.250
Huh?! Why should I do that?!

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.090
Well, you just said I can't leave.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.480
If someone doesn't get it for me, 
I'm gonna die of starvation.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.630
Just eat something else. 
Why does it have to be—

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.820
Spicy pollock roe is a Hakata specialty!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:34.950
What kind of life would it be if you couldn't 
eat spicy pollock roe with white rice?!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:38.910
No matter what anyone else might say, 
it's my number one soul food!

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.450
So can you go get it for me?

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.460
I'll be a good boy if you do.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.830
Just keep the door locked,

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.080
and don't open it, no matter 
who comes along!

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:52.890
Got it?!

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.050
You can keep the change.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.310
Now, then...

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:06.190
Why are there so many different kinds?

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.400
It's just spicy pollock roe!

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.400
Spicy Pollock Roe

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.340
His name is Lin Xianming.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.330
On paper, he's Taiwanese,

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.960
but he was apparently born 
in a Chinese farming village.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:22.980
Lin-kun, huh?

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.680
I haven't figured out who hired him,

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.770
but based on his history,

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:30.300
my guess would be some Chinese organization.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:34.260
That means they're likely to be 
the organization backing Miroir.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.560
And the mystery person 
with the mayor in this photo

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.460
is also involved in that organization.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.170
Good, good.

00:07:42.170 --> 00:07:44.720
Oh, I have one prediction.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:48.440
I bet this Lin Xianming-kun is getting 
himself a shiner right about now.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.160
What the hell, dude?!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:57.320
Nice. I like that look on your face.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.870
I love kids with attitude.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.610
Not bad.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.320
So you want to kill me before getting to him?

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.770
Challenge accepted.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:18.600
No, my only job was that one punch.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.820
Huh?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.460
Later.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.560
Hey, wait a minute!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.000
Aren't you a hitman hired by Zhang?

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.440
Who's that?

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.650
I was hired by an avenger.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.070
You punched a club worker 
yesterday, didn't you?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.240
Oh.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.110
He's the client.

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:37.930
Because you punched him,

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:40.070
you got a punch back.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.830
Avengers don't do more to the target 
than was done to the client.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.370
Oh, but...

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.930
This is actually my part-time job.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.090
<b>Chiropractor</b>

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.140
My real job is...

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.250
<b>Torturer</b>

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.280
A torturer?

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:56.640
I haven't gotten a lot of torture jobs lately.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.830
If you have anyone you 
want tortured, call me.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.620
Later.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.560
Yamato-kun wanted revenge?

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.090
Yeah, that's why he asked 
me to look the guy up.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.770
He left me the wallet he swiped from him.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:14.370
I was surprised when, just as 
I was wrapping up my search,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.780
you sent me a photo of the same guy.

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.950
Yeah, that would be a surprise, all right.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.850
Revenge should have been exacted by now.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.680
Give him back his wallet, will you?

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:28.460
Oh, and tell him to ditch his receipts.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:32.470
You can find out a lot of things by 
matching up the date and time

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:34.420
on a receipt with surveillance footage.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:38.120
I see.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.200
What's this?

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:40.890
No clue.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:44.350
I haven't looked into it. Maybe
it's his little sister or something.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.980
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:53.360
Oops...

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.320
You bastard. You left anyway.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.650
I had to go to the bat-cages.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:02.280
I mean, to the batting cages.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.150
Well, as you can see, I'm safe and sound.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:05.620
Of course you are.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.330
Because...

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:13.000
The killer was trying to ambush you here.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.630
Oh, my.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.600
I wonder what I should do with you.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:22.970
How about I cut your head off 
and mail it back to your client?

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:25.430
Let him go.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:26.500
Huh?!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.190
Tell him to pay me already!

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:37.570
He'd better not send losers like 
that guy in my stead again.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:41.530
Oh, by the way, where's 
the spicy pollock roe?

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.450
Here.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.060
Hey, this is from Fukusaya!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.420
I said Fukuya, didn't I?!

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.740
What's the difference?!

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:55.130
It's only off by two letters.

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:59.090
Would you say that to an 
Ito-san and a Saito-san?

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.410
Whatever!

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:04.840
Oh, you left your wallet there.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.800
You useless moron!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.860
Why can't you kill a kid like him?!

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.820
It seems we're both plagued by problems.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.910
My apologies. I didn't intend 
for you to witness that.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:28.410
So, you want a woman?

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:32.790
I had intended to have her work at Miroir,

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.960
but I've decided to offer her to you instead.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.530
As per your request, she has no family.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:42.180
No one would raise any alarm 
if she were to vanish.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.640
Here's the money.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.550
No, there's no need for that.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:50.310
What is it that you want, then?

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.770
There's this kid who used 
to be a hitman of mine.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:57.470
I want your people to get rid of him.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:59.230
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:01.700
It's a little late, but here's breakfast.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.160
Huh?

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.370
<b>Hakata
Tonkotsu</b>

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.370
<b>Ramen</b>

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.240
Weren't you gonna eat spicy pollock roe?

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.060
That's for later.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.480
I haven't made rice yet.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:12.610
Why haven't you?

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:14.530
Eating ramen for breakfast...

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:16.330
What? What's wrong with that?

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.810
It's not good.

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:20.610
Besides, I hate tonkotsu ramen.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.050
It's so oily that it just sits in my stomach.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.910
You're still going to eat it, though.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:28.000
Can't waste food.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.440
I have a policy of never wasting food.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:33.060
How noble of you.

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:35.750
Oh, it's ready.

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:41.490
Hey, have you ever eaten food 
that's fallen on the ground?

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:44.200
Nope.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:46.910
Thought so.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:50.520
Well, I'm digging in.

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:52.080
Right, same.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:00.000
It's good.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:03.400
Right?

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:18.440
You're finally awake!

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.820
Don't look at me like that.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.290
You're ruining your pretty face.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:25.490
Let's play.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:28.450
For a long, long time.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.410
So after a lifetime of loneliness,

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.070
she ends up on that shithead's bed...

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:37.230
Hey, stop playing with the grenade.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.000
Fine.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:40.420
Ivanov.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:44.610
In exchange for the woman, 
the organization wants us to do a job.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.790
A former hitman of theirs.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.480
Will you take it on?

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:49.680
Sure.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.090
Killing a hitman? Cool.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.750
That's like the Niwaka Samurai.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:57.410
I hear about this "Niwaka 
Samurai" all the time,

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:59.690
but what does the "Niwaka" 
part refer to, anyway?

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.940
Who knows?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:04.570
Niwaka is a traditional form of 
theater they perform here in Hakata.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.240
There's a kind of mask they use for it,

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:13.400
and the killer is called that because he 
wears that mask and wields a katana.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:20.500
They say that everyone who's 
seen him has been killed.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.610
Huh... But if they were all killed,

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.670
no one should know about him, right?

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:27.960
Rumors.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:30.760
All just rumors.

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:34.220
<b>Hotel New Hakata</b>

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:34.220
Hello?

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.900
<i>Hey, I just wanted to congratulate you.</i>

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:38.900
Huh? What for?

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:41.460
<i>Oh, about Murase Jun, of course.</i>

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:43.820
<i>You killed him and made it 
look like a traffic accident.</i>

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.190
<i>Style points for that.</i>

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.320
Huh?

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:49.640
<i>I've already sent you the payment, 
so check that you got it.</i>

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:56.120
Hello, this is Bar Babylon.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.090
Oh, Saito-chan.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.330
Huh? Murase Jun?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.730
Yes, he's dead.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:06.300
He died this morning around 4 AM with 
two friends of his in a traffic accident.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.760
<b>DUI? Three College 
Students Dead</b>

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.760
Were you involved?

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:12.760
<i>I was with you at the time, 
so it couldn't have been me.</i>

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:14.510
Right...

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.650
Hey, hang on a second.

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.100
Did you say two others died with him?

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.120
<i>Yes, they were all friends in college.</i>

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.690
If I recall, there were three 
attackers in that assault...

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.560
Huh?

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.580
<i>Oh, never mind.</i>

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.690
<i>Anyway, I wasn't involved.</i>

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.010
Sorry to bother you.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.130
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.700
<i>Call me anytime.</i>

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.700
<b>DUI? Three College 
Students Dead</b>

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.700
So it wasn't just an accident...

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.940
I don't think it was.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.960
Maybe it was to silence them.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:47.380
The victim said someone gave orders 
to the three attackers, didn't he?

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:48.760
Right!

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:51.300
<b>Yotsui Bank Online Banking 
Service Login Page</b>

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:55.370
I wonder if I should return the money...

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.050
Huh?

00:15:57.650 --> 00:15:58.930
What?!

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.350
At least today...

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.020
Motsu hot pot is the best!

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:09.730
Iron pan gyoza is the best!

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:12.650
Tonkotsu ramen is the best!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.460
Hakata is the best!

00:16:19.010 --> 00:16:21.410
Titty bars are the best...

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:23.830
<i>The catcher misses the throw!</i>

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.550
<i>And the runner on third 
is making a run for home!</i>

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.790
<i>They've tied the game!</i>

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.790
Yeah!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:30.100
<i>The runner from second 
is now at third base, too!</i>

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:33.340
<i>Will the ball make it to 
home in time?! It didn't!</i>

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.970
Score!

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.970
<i>The catcher's error led to
an incredible two-run hit!</i>

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.890
<i>The Hawks have turned the tables!</i>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:42.570
In baseball, you never know 
what's going to happen until

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:44.690
you're in the ninth with 
two outs and three strikes.

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.500
Yup, yup.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.540
It's not a bad thing to have spicy pollock 
roe from a different place now and then.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.360
This one's got a good kick to it.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.130
Don't you think?

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:58.840
It's really annoying when 
they change the TV schedule.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.040
<b>Due to the baseball game going into extra innings,
the serial drama "Love Once in a Lifetime" will air at 9:30 PM. 
Thank you for your understanding.</b>

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:03.040
You're a hitman who likes romantic dramas?

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.370
It's not like that.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.620
It's just that when you're 
in this line of work,

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:11.550
sometimes you want a glimpse at 
what regular people's lives look like.

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:13.180
Huh...

00:17:15.190 --> 00:17:17.510
By the way, Lin Xianming-kun...

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:25.880
How do you know my name?

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:27.410
I looked you up.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.450
Well, you <i>are</i> a private eye, I guess.

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:33.330
I have some questions for you.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.240
Will you answer them honestly?

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.410
Depends on the question.

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:41.540
Why'd you become a hitman?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.150
For money, obviously.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:46.430
Are you in debt?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.120
Basically, yeah.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:53.630
And what if I said I'd pay 
off your debt for you?

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.380
Let's strike a deal.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.760
I'll pay you a good price 
for your information.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:04.970
Five million.

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:08.010
That's what I need to be free.

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.980
Is cash okay?

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.760
So, question.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.880
What's the name of the 
organization that hired you?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.750
Kakyu Association.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:25.700
It's a bunch of yakuza who were exiled, 
plus the Chinese mafia.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:29.640
Oh, one of those multinational 
mafia groups that's on the rise, then.

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:31.930
What's their main source of revenue?

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:33.490
Drugs? Weapons?

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.520
People.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:37.480
Human trafficking...

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:40.690
I don't know the details since 
I'm not directly involved.

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:43.560
I just get jobs and kill people.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:48.270
Then do you know who this is?

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.230
I saw him once.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.650
He's Longfang Wang, the 
head of the organization.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:57.410
I see.

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:01.400
That'd explain why the mayor wouldn't 
want anyone seeing them together.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.410
Can I ask you a few more questions?

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.620
Like I said, depends on the question.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.490
Huh? Why am I naked?

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.840
N-No way... Did I...

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:26.510
U-Um, sorry...

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.780
She's dead! She's dead!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:39.210
She's dead! She's dead!

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.030
There you go. Five million.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:46.680
You said you'd be free.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.790
What will you do now that 
your debt's paid off?

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.770
I'm going back home.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.550
Got someone waiting for you there?

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:55.030
That's none of your business.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:59.550
If you have any trouble, 
feel free to call me anytime.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.710
I'll help you.

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:05.260
There's nothing for you to help me with.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.010
You don't get it, do you?

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.930
What do you think a hitman needs?

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:11.990
Huh?

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:14.400
Strength, of course.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.950
That's incorrect.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:19.700
Here's a hint: you need it in baseball, too.

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.690
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:30.260
Weirdo.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:40.070
Now do you feel like apologizing?

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:41.370
<i>Nope.</i>

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:43.260
<i>I got the five million.</i>

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:44.440
Oh?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.730
I can pay off my debt now.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:50.660
I'm a free man.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:53.800
<i>I guess you haven't heard, then.</i>

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.980
Huh?

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:59.900
<b>Chinese Student Found Dead</b>

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:59.900
<i>A woman's body was found this 
morning in a hotel in Fukuoka City.</i>

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:02.750
<i>The woman is believed to be</i>

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:07.240
<i>a Chinese student who had been
living in Fukuoka, Lin Qiaomei-san.</i>

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:07.240
<b>Lin Qiaomei-san</b>

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:13.140
<i>The police are looking for the man who 
was sharing the room with the victim.</i>

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:17.590
Lin... Qiaomei...

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:21.210
Brother!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.920
Brother!

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:38.280
<i>Sounds like you just found out.</i>

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:48.570
<b>Lin Qiaomei-san</b>

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:41.690
<i>Yes, that's your little sister, all right.</i>

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:44.150
<i>She came on our books three years ago.</i>

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:48.560
<i>A good buyer showed up 
as soon as she came here.</i>

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:50.970
<i>If only you'd been a little more cooperative,</i>

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:55.080
<i>we may have been able to 
work out a joyous reunion...</i>

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:57.000
I'll kill you.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:02.300
I'll kill you and the bastard 
who did this to Qiaomei!

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:04.410
You're dead meat!

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:05.270
Give me a name!

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:06.350
Spicy pollock roe works.

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:08.480
The avenger has accepted the job.

00:23:08.480 --> 00:23:09.950
I'll take that job.

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:12.610
Of course I would never show up empty-handed.

00:23:12.610 --> 00:23:14.990
Hakata folks are busybodies.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
#03 Teamwork
